<speak>I like the idea of attaching it to something I already do. Whenever I introduce a completely new system, I follow it very enthusiastically for a week and then forget about it. The same happened with the office cupboards. I bought labels, sorted everything, and explained the arrangement to everyone. Then one urgent delivery came along, someone put a folder in the nearest empty space, and gradually the old habits returned. My nephew says we should make the easy place the correct place. That is a good way of putting it. If personal papers have one obvious home, I might actually keep them there.</speak>